Part 1: KEY FINDINGS
The Population and Household tables included in this Volume 2 Basic Table report were derived from the
Solomon Island 2019 Population and Housing Census. Significantly, these statistical tables are useful for wider
audience but specifically meant for users  with statistical background such as planners and policy makers,
researches, specialists, and donor representatives.
The set of tables presented here adhere to the United Nations principles and recommendations for population and
housing censuses to ensure a consistent standard of comparabilit y with the previous census. Inclusion of new
tables are included thus make changes to the numbering, ordering and table titles of tables in each group. It is
important to note that numbering of each person table links to the chapters in Volume 1 Census report. Therefore,
table 1 starts with P2.1 in which P stands for “Persons” , 2 represent the Geography chapter in Volume 1 report
and 1 shows the first table of Geography chapter and presented in ascending order. Whilst numbering of
household tables starts with H1 where ‘H’ stands for Household.
The Volume 2 Basic Table report contains 105 tables in total distributed into fifteen (15) subject matters. The
person tables comprises of 70 tables and 35 tables household tables. The main subject matter topics are:
1. Geography
2. Age structure
3. Population Dynamics
4. Urbanisation
5. Fertility
6. Mortality
7. Migration
8. Social Characteristic
9. Education and Literacy
10. Disability
11. Communication and Internet
12. Economic and Labour Force
13. Formal and Informal Sectors
14. Household and Housing
15. Constituency Development Fund

